          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='5814' id='6' type-v2='text' w='77333' x='1636' y='465'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='24' underline='true'>Key Insights and Recommendations</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='90116' id='7' type-v2='text' w='44727' x='2606' y='8953'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>Business Key Insights</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff0000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Single Family drives the market.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'> 80% of sale value comes from one category — Condos and multi-family are a much smaller, less active segment.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff0000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Growth is market-wide, not town-specific.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Æ </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>No town exceeds ~4% share, so this isn&apos;t a &quot;find the next boomtown&quot; story — it&apos;s a broad trend, meaning opportunity should be spread, not concentrated.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff0000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Growth is slowing.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>YoY growth fell from 17.16% (2021) to 9.42% (2022). Positive, but the deceleration matters more than the peak — don&apos;t plan around 2021 momentum.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff0000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Assessed values track sale prices well</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Æ </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>(ratio near 1.0), making assessed value a reasonably reliable pricing reference — once outlier transactions are excluded from the data.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='90581' id='8' type-v2='text' w='50545' x='49030' y='7907'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='20'>Business Recommendations</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff0000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>Prioritize Single Family homes.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>They drive 80% of total sale value — the clear focus for investment or development budget over Condos and multi-family types.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff0000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>Diversify across towns, don&apos;t chase a &quot;hot&quot; market</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>No town exceeds ~4% share — growth is broad-based, not concentrated, so spread presence rather than betting on one location.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff0000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>Move cautiously — growth is slowing.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>Æ </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>YoY growth fell from 17.16% (2021) to 9.42% (2022). Confirm the trend continues before committing to large capital positions.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff0000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>Use Sales Ratio for pricing checks — after cleaning the data.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#ff0000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>Æ </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Trebuchet MS' fontsize='18'>A ratio near 1.0 flags fairly priced properties, but non-arm&apos;s-length sales (e.g., $1 transfers) must be excluded first, or the tool will misfire.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
